    "title": "SENIOR SCENE | Local disasters",
    "text": "Reading the news about the abundant wild fires across the continent and it's devastating aftermath is stunning. I live in the middle of forested land and worry through droughts. Arkansas rates in the top 10 states of home fires. Regardless of the season it's a constant crisis here.\nThis week we have seen three families from local fires needing immediate assistance in all areas. They need clothes, household items, medicines, transportation, and much more. Every situation is different.\nI am so proud that Jackson House doesn't insist you fit into a box of services. Instead we wrap you in a warm hug, adjusting our resources to fit your needs. The difference is massive!\nIf you want to have a 50+ year legacy of solving emergency situations helping people in crisis, Jackson House is your place. At JH \"Every Item, Every Dollar, Every Person, Counts\". 501-623-4048 http://jacksonhouse.org\n———\nSource: Advertiser submitted\nYou're one step away from the full story.\nLog in or create an account to continue reading.",
